
# The abstract database native module: the signatures the public `base/db` re-exports. The build rewrites this to the
# target's impl (`native/node/db`, Postgres-backed; `native/swift/db` and `native/kotlin/db`, SQLite-backed; and in
# a cask's page, the generated `native/webview/db`, which carries each call over the bridge) via the native-env
# mechanism. A `row` is an opaque result row. Every task is async, because inside a cask each one is a message
# to the process that holds the database, and an API that is sync on one platform and async on another is two APIs.

# an opaque result row (a dynamic record from the database)
form row
  link handle, mark private

task connect
  take url, like text
  note async

task query
  take sql, like text
  take params
    like list
      like unknown
  like list
    like row
  note async

task run
  take sql, like text
  take params
    like list
      like unknown
  note async

task field
  take row, like row
  take name, like text
  like text
  note async
